{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken","id":28055,"title":"Gender dynamics in Forsaken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-11T09:43:05-08:00","id":28055,"title":"Gender dynamics in Forsaken","content":"I recently read these interesting posts (<a href=\"http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/2013/03/werewolves-they-just-cant-help-it.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/20...t-help-it.html</a>,<a href=\"http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/2012/05/problem-with-female-werewolves.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/20...erewolves.html</a> ) about the troubling way werewolf relationships are portrayed in Urban Fantasy (I'm looking at you, Adam Hauptman, you possessive control freak you), and I was wondering if the community thinks Forsaken manages to avoid the most common pitfalls.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the setting does. True, werewolves have anger management issues (to put it mildly), but it's portrayed as a serious problem that often prevents werewolves from having normal family lives, instead of &quot;aw, look how protective he is.&quot; Also, I detect none of the whole &quot;female werewolves are subjugated by the males&quot; trope that seems depressingly common. In Forsaken, alphas are as likely to be female as male. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1631,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","user":"Karthak","date":". 12-11-2013, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:05:56-08:00","id":28068,"title":"","content":"Well, the part about &quot;possession&quot; thing goes right out the window because Uratha are not to breed with each other, so there's none of that &quot;SHE'S MINE!&quot; crap.<br /> <br /> The other part, they are multiple sample packs with females in charge and even a couple of all female packs, and no one treats them as &quot;lesser&quot; without regretting it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, yeah, not really there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 12-11-2013, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:13:02-08:00","id":28074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken#post28055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think the setting does. True, werewolves have anger management issues (to put it mildly), but it's portrayed as a serious problem that often prevents werewolves from having normal family lives, instead of &quot;aw, look how protective he is.&quot; Also, I detect none of the whole &quot;female werewolves are subjugated by the males&quot; trope that seems depressingly common. In Forsaken, alphas are as likely to be female as male. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the War Form is just as powerful if a female uratha is using it as a male and the fact that the Forsaken are lead by a crazy ass moon spirit who takes the image of patron Goddess in their tales, It would be safe to say that gender isn't that much of an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:46:12-08:00","id":28095,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I think those concerns are more for the paranormal romance genre than the sort of stories Forsaken aims to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:57:56-08:00","id":28104,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I -could- see this with a Forsaken and their wolf-blooded mate.<br /> <br /> But in general, Forsaken are more based on actual wolves. And actual wolves do not have alphas in their packs, since its parents+kids that makes the pack. So the posessiveness would be less controlling and more protective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:59:38-08:00","id":28105,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once again, the animal nature is blamed for violence against women and it\u2019s all okay because there\u2019s woo woo involved.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The core book does seem to discuss the likelihood of domestic abuse. &quot;For example, a werewolf can be driven into Death Rage by discovering that her boyfriend has been cheating on her, only to come to her senses covered in his blood and torn flesh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather that Death Rage by way of sexual jealousy not be emphasized in the new chronicle book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:46:36-08:00","id":28217,"title":"","content":"Can't see the problem here. Werewolf is supposed to be a game about horror and drama, right? The game certainly doesn't do anything to whitewash or romanticize abusive behaviour of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T14:04:59-08:00","id":28290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28104#post28104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I -could- see this with a Forsaken and their wolf-blooded mate</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Though it isn't a gendered issue with the Forsaken. As well, Forsaken doesn't really play this as a positive thing. Long term Uratha-Wolfblooded relationships are treated as inherently risky because of the constant risk of abusive behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28105#post28105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd rather that Death Rage by way of sexual jealousy not be emphasized in the new chronicle book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the core book overly emphasized this. It's an example of the kind of mundane emotional trauma that can trigger irrational violence in normal real world people and how that ends even more tragically for the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I don't want pages on the subject, but you can't escape this issue. Forsaken puts a heavy emphasis on trying to balance spirit and human natures. It has to make maintaining your human side difficult and threatening. It's hard to image a more direct and visceral illustration of that struggle than having a deep loving bond with someone while at the same time knowing that you're a ticking time-bomb of uncontrollable violence.<br /> <br /> It isn't about making werewolves to be walking domestic violence metaphors by having them be constantly possessive, controlling, and demanding of those they love. It's about creating a much more personal ethical dilemma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T14:18:06-08:00","id":28299,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't see it. Like the guy above said it seems those articles are more about paranormal romance than horror games.<br /> <br /> But even then, for every instance I can think of where a werewolf would be overly possessive or abusive or sexist, examples could exist for either gender and doesn't exist as an across-the-board standard for all werewolves any more than it does for all people in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-11-2013, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T15:07:35-08:00","id":28326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28104#post28104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I -could- see this with a Forsaken and their wolf-blooded mate.<br /> <br /> But in general, Forsaken are more based on actual wolves. And actual wolves do not have alphas in their packs, since its parents+kids that makes the pack. So the posessiveness would be less controlling and more protective.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they're not. Forsaken packs are (usually) a bunch of strangers since Werewolves can't bread with each other and they very much do have an Alpha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T15:44:54-08:00","id":28349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28326#post28326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they're not. Forsaken packs are (usually) a bunch of strangers since Werewolves can't bread with each other and they very much do have an Alpha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was unclear ^^''<br /> <br /> I meant that their behaviour in general is based more on actual wolves. Not their pack structure, which IS more closer to the forced zoo example that gets called the alpha thing.<br /> <br /> But relationships with wolf-blooded would not be based on that system, hopefullt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T19:29:16-08:00","id":28472,"title":"","content":"I don't read romance books let alone horror themed ones. But this all seems rather confusing to me. I assume most of the reader base for romance is female. If women didn't like this kind of thing you would think things like 50 shades of grey wouldn't be bestsellers. Plus the author of that article uses Anita Blake as a example in on of the paragraphs. But from what I have been told she has a harem of men that she forces one way monogamy on. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T22:56:10-08:00","id":28556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28472#post28472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't read romance books let alone horror themed ones. But this all seems rather confusing to me. I assume most of the reader base for romance is female. If women didn't like this kind of thing you would think things like 50 shades of grey wouldn't be bestsellers. Plus the author of that article uses Anita Blake as a example in on of the paragraphs. But from what I have been told she has a harem of men that she forces one way monogamy on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a good idea to generalize what women like like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T23:08:10-08:00","id":28558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28556#post28556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's a good idea to generalize what women like like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not a good idea. It's pretty bad, in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T01:46:02-08:00","id":28594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28556#post28556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's a good idea to generalize what women like like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.rwa.org/p/cm/ld/fid=582\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.rwa.org/assets/site/logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rwa.org/p/cm/ld/fid=582\" target=\"_blank\"> Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rwa.org/p/cm/ld/fid=582\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.rwa.org/p/cm/ld/fid=582 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Women make up 91 percent of romance book buyers, and men make up 9 percent.&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">&quot;The sexy &quot;Twilight&quot; fan fiction that follows naive college graduate </span></span><b>Anastasia Steele</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> and the handsome, dominant billionaire </span></span><b>Christian Grey</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> has </span></span><a href=\"http://www.businessinsider.com/amazons-kindle-made-it-ok-for-women-to-read-porn-on-the-subway-2012-6\" target=\"_blank\">transformed the way women are reading porn</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2014</span></span><a href=\"http://www.entertainmentwise.com/news/79565/EL-James-50-Shades-Of-Grey-Breaks-Kindle-Records-With-1m-Sales\" target=\"_blank\">the book just became the first to sell more than 1 million copies on the Amazon Kindle</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Read more: <a href=\"http://www.businessinsider.com/by-the-numbers-the-50-shades-of-grey-phenomenon-2012-6?op=1#ixzz2nFgwxKMT\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.businessinsider.com/by-th...#ixzz2nFgwxKMT</a><br /> <br /> I'm not insulting anybody. It seems women like these kind of stories. They are the target audience and seem to enjoy reading it. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T04:04:18-08:00","id":28617,"title":"","content":"I don't see how that post generalises women, it looks like it generalised romance novels; and I guess it generalised them accurately, RWA seems authoritative.<br /> <br /> And I kinda share zap's confusion. I don't read romance either, but the idea books revealing in romantic troupes that should be avoided in the real world just seems... normal to me. I mean, look at the stuff I read and how many sci-fi or fantasy things end with the good guy dethroning the evil overlord with violence. Superman's qualifications for being a hero is moral virtue and punching people really hard; one of those is not really a good thing in the real world (and Iron Man, Wolverine, Batman, etc only have the punching people part).<br /> <br /> Fiction revealing in stuff that we wouldn't want in our lives just seems perfectly normal and healthy to me. I don't see what the article was complaining about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T07:22:05-08:00","id":28711,"title":"","content":"Sorry, gotta back zap up on this one - I used to work in a book store and you didn't see a lot of guys buying those books, and I have yet to see a copy 50 Shades of Shit in the hands of anyone but a woman.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, it's trite because it's true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 12-12-2013, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:45:53-08:00","id":28777,"title":"","content":"Great. 4th part of the saga. 50 Shades of Shit.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot, Bear.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:47:15-08:00","id":28779,"title":"","content":"No problem, here to help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T11:36:46-08:00","id":28842,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with Zap's statement is not that the vast majority of romance literature (in the USA) is bought by women. That's fact (though a quick side rant, it is a culturally reinforced piece of bullshit because it attempts to enforce a gendered divide by putting &quot;male&quot; consumption of erotic material in the category of porn and &quot;female&quot; consumption of erotic material into romance literature; thereby completely skewing any relevance this might have on if there's any real gendered difference in the amount consumption of erotica and reinforcing negative gendered stereotypes).<br /> <br /> The problem is then generalizing that back onto what all women like (&quot; If women didn't like this kind of thing you would think things like 50 shades of grey wouldn't be bestsellers.&quot;). Just because most of the consumers of a product are women doesn't mean that most women like that product. All it means is that there's an audience amongst women than enjoy reading books that contain these elements.<br /> <br /> As for the article in the OP:<br /> <br /> I think the problem is that &quot;werewolf&quot; becomes a cover for not being responsible with &quot;edgy&quot; material. Rather than writing fiction that either (a) establishes a healthy power dynamic between a couple that includes the altered psychology of being a werewolf or (b) deals with the unhealthy power dynamic being romanticized as being ultimately unhealthy, there is a growing acceptance of just tagging a character as a werewolf and lazily ignoring having to deal with pesky things like characterization and relationship dynamics.<br /> <br /> Basically, there is a crop of urban fantasy romance literature that uses &quot;werewolf&quot; to disguise abusive relationships. Is there an audience for that? Sure. But that audience would probably be just as happy to consume erotica that does a better job of dealing with these topics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:11:36-08:00","id":28918,"title":"","content":"First of all I didn't read Zap as &quot;generalising back onto what all women like&quot;, but I'm sure Zap can say what that post meant better than I.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now on behalf of myself. I quite simply don't see any problem with the way these authors are portraying so called &quot;edgy&quot; material. It's lazy and ignores relationship dynamics, so what? In <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airport_novel\" target=\"_blank\">certain circumstances</a> lazy and clich\u00e9d writing has an advantage over deep, innovative and thought provoking work. In fact I would go so far as to say that your last paragraph is wrong. If there was paranormal romance that creates a more nuanced and three-dimensional portrayal of werewolf romance I suspect people would read both. Lots of people watched both Thor: The Dark World and Full Metal jacket. The existence of media that does a better job at dealing with edgy topics like war hasn't diminished the market for light entertaining action flicks.<br /> <br /> Nor do I think there's anything wrong with making entertainment out of unhealthy relationships; if you think so the burden of proof is on you to demonstrate that these possessive werewolf relationships are causing actual harm. Until it's been published in a respected academic journal and confirmed by peer review I'm going to put it on the pile with: Rock and roll, heavy metal, comic books, video games, <a href=\"http://outofthejungle.blogspot.co.uk/2007/11/socrates-objections-to-writing.html\" target=\"_blank\">writing</a> and every other form of media that was suspected of corrupting the youth but ultimately turned out to be perfectly harmless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-12-2013, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:56:13-08:00","id":28950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28918#post28918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all I didn't read Zap as &quot;generalising back onto what all women like&quot;, but I'm sure Zap can say what that post meant better than I.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can accept that is not Zap's intended meaning. However the statement I quoted certainly generalizes back. He doesn't qualify &quot;women&quot; in any way that narrows if from &quot;all women&quot; to &quot;some women.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airport_novel\" target=\"_blank\">certain circumstances</a> lazy and clich\u00e9d writing has an advantage over deep, innovative and thought provoking work. </div> </div> </div>And yet, you cite a category that is much more associated with non-romance literature. And airport novel is not synonymous with lazy or cliched writing. It is characterized by being fast paced and engaging. The whole point is that they're a good way to kill a few hours while you're stuck in the airport. They make heavy use of tropes to facilitate that role, but isn't the same as your claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there was paranormal romance that creates a more nuanced and three-dimensional portrayal of werewolf romance I suspect people would read both. </div> </div> </div>None of the people I know into paranormal romance go back once they find an author they like that does better treatment of these issues. The two authors I'm familiar with through their fans that put out what I would consider more nuanced works have had massive trouble getting through to the larger audience because of something that happens in most media industries: inertia. Big publishers would rather another bodice-ripper that they can predict accurately on sales than take risks on &quot;new&quot; approaches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lots of people watched both Thor: The Dark World and Full Metal jacket. </div> </div> </div>Apples and oranges there. FMJ and Thor aren't competing in anywhere near the same space in cinema. But if you look at the Batman Begins trilogy and the new MCU they have changed the game for superhero movies. The new Robocop film is already heading towards a belly-flop by not paying enough attention to what made those franchises successful. I'm sure people will watch the new Robocop anyway, but I doubt it is going to better than a &quot;meh&quot; from everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor do I think there's anything wrong with making entertainment out of unhealthy relationships; </div> </div> </div>I'm going to stop you there and get you off your high horse. I never said there was. I said there's something wrong with making entertainment out of unhealthy relationships then white-washing the unhealthy parts of the relationship with the &quot;werewolf&quot; tag.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T15:11:40-08:00","id":28958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28842#post28842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is then generalizing that back onto what all women like (&quot; If women didn't like this kind of thing you would think things like 50 shades of grey wouldn't be bestsellers.&quot;). Just because most of the consumers of a product are women doesn't mean that most women like that product. <b>All it means is that there's an audience amongst women than enjoy reading books that contain these elements</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right As long as they enjoy it I see nothing wrong with it. I mean I read American Psycho and enjoyed it. But it didn't make me treat women any differently nor did I get more creative with my meatloaf recipes. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28842#post28842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the problem is that &quot;werewolf&quot; becomes a cover for not being responsible with &quot;edgy&quot; material. Rather than writing fiction that either (a) establishes a healthy power dynamic between a couple that includes the altered psychology of being a werewolf or (b) deals with the unhealthy power dynamic being romanticized as being ultimately unhealthy, there is a growing acceptance of just tagging a character as a werewolf and lazily ignoring having to deal with pesky things like characterization and relationship dynamics.<br /> <br /> <b>Basically, there is a crop of urban fantasy romance literature that uses &quot;werewolf&quot; to disguise abusive relationships</b>. Is there an audience for that? Sure. But that audience would probably be just as happy to consume erotica that does a better job of dealing with these topics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know but if this is your problem then maybe the article does have a point. There is a picture in blood of the wolf on page 105 that sums up pretty well what a relationship in any context with a werewolf is like in this setting. But I very rarely see people bringing this kind of stuff into the game anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T16:07:26-08:00","id":28977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28958#post28958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a picture in blood of the wolf on page 105 that sums up pretty well what a relationship in any context with a werewolf is like in this setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plainly-dressed woman with a hammer looking around while being watched by a weird corpsey thing and a weird shadowy spider thing.<br /> <br /> A metaphor, perhaps.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">You possibly mean page 10<i>9</i>, which has a naked werewolf man swinging down into a bedroom window.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T16:57:49-08:00","id":29007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28977#post28977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plainly-dressed woman with a hammer looking around while being watched by a weird corpsey thing and a weird shadowy spider thing.<br /> <br /> A metaphor, perhaps.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">You possibly mean page 10<i>9</i>, which has a naked werewolf man swinging down into a bedroom window.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>.Right my bad. I have the pdf version and was using the page count on the taskbar. I mean the picture on page 102.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1303,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","user":"zap rowsdower","date":". 12-12-2013, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T18:44:01-08:00","id":29068,"title":"","content":"Most readers of Twilight and Fifty Shades of Grey are women, but not most women read the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T18:45:35-08:00","id":29069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28105#post28105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'd rather that Death Rage by way of sexual jealousy not be emphasized in the new chronicle book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a difference between &quot;sexual jealousy&quot; and active betrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:18:51-08:00","id":29093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29068#post29068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most readers of Twilight and Fifty Shades of Grey are women, but not most women read the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>My objection was one of semantics, which I feel this addresses eloquently. Thank you, Isator!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:28:28-08:00","id":29095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28105#post28105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once again, the animal nature is blamed for violence against women and it\u2019s all okay because there\u2019s woo woo involved.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The core book does seem to discuss the likelihood of domestic abuse. &quot;For example, a werewolf can be driven into Death Rage by discovering that her boyfriend has been cheating on her, only to come to her senses covered in his blood and torn flesh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather that Death Rage by way of sexual jealousy not be emphasized in the new chronicle book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing in WtF, is that when those elements come up, they are actually played as horrific, not as &quot;well it's ok because of your animal instincts.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:37:19-08:00","id":29097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29095#post29095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing in WtF, is that when those elements come up, they are actually played as horrific, not as &quot;well it's ok because of your animal instincts.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. I still choose not to emphasize that theme in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:38:08-08:00","id":29098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28472#post28472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't read romance books let alone horror themed ones. But this all seems rather confusing to me. I assume most of the reader base for romance is female. If women didn't like this kind of thing you would think things like 50 shades of grey wouldn't be bestsellers. Plus the author of that article uses Anita Blake as a example in on of the paragraphs. But from what I have been told she has a harem of men that she forces one way monogamy on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The people who like it are mostly women != women (as a vast manifold demo) like it. There is plenty of misogynist media consumed by women.<br /> <br /> Which is not to condemn the genre. I have specific problems with Twilight regurgitating rape culture (and any self respecting 16 year old fangirl can tell you there is WAY better porn out there than 50 Shades of Grey), but a large part of &quot;paranormal romance&quot; being harshly judged itself is rooted in misogynistic attitudes toward &quot;things women like&quot; - that results in things demographically favored by women being dismissed as of lesser value compared to things demographically favored by men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T21:32:45-08:00","id":29141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28958#post28958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right As long as they enjoy it I see nothing wrong with it. I mean I read American Psycho and enjoyed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>People enjoying media doesn't excuse media that adds to the whole rape-culture problem. Normalization works on everyone.<br /> <br /> As for American Psycho? I'm glad you enjoyed it. It's a good book. But I find it hard to believe that anyone that's read it thinks of it as a happy romp on the awesomeness of being a yuppie maniac. Bateman is a horrible person; regardless of what is true and what isn't behind the wall of his flawed perspective. He is a larger critique of the culture the author perceives as having spawned him; which is pretty much the only sympathetic thing about him. Nothing about his life is portrayed as being a good thing; it isn't even portrayed as being an excusable thing. The basic question of the novel is, &quot;what is wrong with a society that cultivates and rewards people like this guy?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I very rarely see people bringing this kind of stuff into the game anyway. </div> </div> </div>That is very true. For most people this isn't the kind of thing they want to actively engage in for an RPG session.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29097#post29097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true. I still choose not to emphasize that theme in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't really a theme. It is an expression of a theme. I don't blame you if you avoid this particular expression, but I think Forsaken would be a bit lacking if you excluded the theme behind it. If there is no inherent tension between werewolves and humans, it damages the attempt to have the werewolves be isolated between two worlds that they are driven to try and balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T01:26:37-08:00","id":29201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28950#post28950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, you cite a category that is much more associated with non-romance literature. And airport novel is not synonymous with lazy or cliched writing. It is characterized by being fast paced and engaging. The whole point is that they're a good way to kill a few hours while you're stuck in the airport. They make heavy use of tropes to facilitate that role, but isn't the same as your claim.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well historical romance is on the list in that wikipedia page; I was also referring to stuff like this: &quot;An airport novel must necessarily be superficially engaging, while not being <u>particularly profound or philosophical</u>, or at least, without such content being necessary for enjoyment of the book&quot;<br /> <br /> I wasn't specifically saying that werewolf romance were airport novels; I was using airport novels as example of books that benefit from being simple page turners with the implication that if under certain circumstances people who normally read &quot;better quality&quot; books would buy airport novels people who normally read &quot;proper romances&quot; might also buy their page turner equivalents under certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28950#post28950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apples and oranges there. FMJ and Thor aren't competing in anywhere near the same space in cinema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... that was my entire point.<br /> <br /> Comparing Pride and Prejudice to Fifty Shades of Grey is like comparing FMJ and Thor. FMJ/Thor are both war films, P&amp;P/FSoG are both about a romantic relationship. Both comparisons are apples and oranges; and clearly there is room in the world for all four of those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28950#post28950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to stop you there and get you off your high horse. I never said there was. I said there's something wrong with making entertainment out of unhealthy relationships <b>then white-washing the unhealthy parts of the relationship with the &quot;werewolf&quot; tag.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> (emphasis mine to show how I read that)<br /> <br /> If I understand you correctly, you're basically saying that Fifty Shades of Grey is fine but Mercy Thompson is not. And the difference between the two is that Mercy Thompson uses werewolf as a justification and FSoG does not...<br /> <br /> Ok...<br /> <br /> You seem like a reasonable person so I'm going to give you the benefit of the doubt. Why is &quot;werewolves&quot; the fundamental problem?<br /> <br /> <br /> [edit]On a second reading, should I have read that as white-washing is the problem? If so, that's what I was responding to the first time when I said I disagreed in my previous post.[edit the second: Ignore this, I posted it too late]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29141#post29141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People enjoying media doesn't excuse media that adds to the whole rape-culture problem. Normalization works on everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm getting back on my &quot;high horse&quot; as you put it.<br /> <br /> As I said in my last post. I have heard people say similar things about every new form of media and so far none of them ended up causing the collapse of morality. There's not even much evidence to say that violent video-games did increase violence. There has been a lot of research into the effects of violent or sexually explicit media and it's inconclusive and frequently studies contradict each other. The idea that stuff like FSoG encourages harmful attitudes in it's readers or society is far from proven.<br /> <br /> The paranormal romance books were written by women writers for a woman audience, I don't understand the appeal but until the evidence against them is much stronger than it is today I'm going to support women in writing and reading whatever they wish. As I would do for anyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Feel free to criticise those books, the poor quality of writing in FSoG is as close to an objective fact as you can get in art, but if you're going to assert that they're harmful I'm going to disagree with you. The evidence just isn't conclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-13-2013, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T02:54:22-08:00","id":29216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29201#post29201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well historical romance is on the list in that wikipedia page; I was also referring to stuff like this: &quot;An airport novel must necessarily be superficially engaging, while not being <u>particularly profound or philosophical</u>, or at least, without such content being necessary for enjoyment of the book&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overly invested in trying to claim I'm looking for some sort of &quot;profound or philosophical&quot; aspect to smut. I'm not asking that erotica be deep. I'm saying that any media, including erotica, should avoid promoting negative cultural institutions and deserves to be called out when it does. <br /> <br /> The difference between a simple page turner and a grand epic is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I understand you correctly, you're basically saying that Fifty Shades of Grey is fine but Mercy Thompson is not. And the difference between the two is that Mercy Thompson uses werewolf as a justification and FSoG does not... </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand. FSoG is trash. It just doesn't compound its errors (ok, it removes those errors when it moved from fanfic to a separate piece inadvertently, the original fanfic hit up this problem plenty) with supernatural excuses.<br /> <br /> FSoG not containing a specific problematic element doesn't mean it doesn't contain plenty of others. Trying to play a &quot;which is worse&quot; game is pointless. Addressing the cultural issues with our current norms is not a matter of specific books, but a matter of addressing larger trends in our media.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is &quot;werewolves&quot; the fundamental problem? </div> </div> </div>It isn't &quot;the&quot; fundamental problem. It is a specific problem in that it is used to disguise abusive behavior as healthy behavior by making it &quot;healthy for werewolves.&quot; Actions that would easily land a human character as a creep (or worse) is suddenly not just ok, but an expression of true love, because it comes from a werewolf rather than a human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have heard people say similar things about every new form of media and so far none of them ended up causing the collapse of morality. </div> </div> </div>Except that's not the claim I'm making.<br /> <br /> First off, there's nothing &quot;new media&quot; here. Erotica is thousands of years old. Stories about supernatural beings having relationships with humans are ancient.<br /> <br /> Second off, this isn't about the collapse of morality. It is about the perpetuation of immorality. Excising institutionalized immoral social norms is not easy. Racism didn't go away when Lincoln have the Gettysburg Address. Racism didn't end when the Civil Rights Act was passed. Ending racism is an ongoing struggle and one of the key components of advancing that struggle is making people aware of racism that they don't realize is racism. Rape culture is no different. Part of addressing rape culture in our society is identifying it for what it is when it comes up. It isn't ok to paint werewolves as good for being possessive of people they're in relationships with. Being possessive is bad. The people in your life are not objects that you own. Chasing away other men from having contact with your female significant other is not an act of love; it is an act of objectification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that stuff like FSoG encourages harmful attitudes in it's readers or society is far from proven. </div> </div> </div>The danger FSoG poses is that anyone that tries to get into actual BDSM relationships with FSoG as a guide is going to hurt themselves (emotionally and/or physically). The problem is that in completely misrepresents what a BDSM relationship actually is and how one is practiced responsibly and safely. Which is an entirely different concern than supernatural beings; werewolves aren't real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Feel free to criticise those books, the poor quality of writing in FSoG is as close to an objective fact as you can get in art, but if you're going to assert that they're harmful I'm going to disagree with you. The evidence just isn't conclusive. </div> </div> </div>Actually the evidence is perfectly conclusive. You're just talking about a completely different kind of harm than I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T03:41:19-08:00","id":29231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29216#post29216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're overly invested in trying to claim I'm looking for some sort of &quot;profound or philosophical&quot; aspect to smut. I'm not asking that erotica be deep.</div> </div> </div> </div> I never said you were. When I brought up airport novels I was referring to a very specific point you made a page ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28842#post28842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that audience would probably be just as happy to consume erotica that does a better job of dealing with these topics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this actually true. This is why I brought up apples and oranges comparisons like FMJ/Thor or P&amp;P/FSoG. I'm guesstimating that any romance novel that handles relationship dynamics in a realistic way would hit a different niche to the current paranormal romances. Just like any film that realistically portrays war hits a different niche to a simple action flick where violence is awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28842#post28842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second off, this isn't about the collapse of morality. It is about the perpetuation of immorality.</div> </div> </div> </div> I fail to see how this is a counter-argument to anything I wrote.<br /> <br /> Whether you call it the collapse of immorality or the perpetuation of immorality is irrelevant, both buzzwords ultimately refer to the same thing: Fantasy media having a negative effect on the real world.<br /> <br /> Violence has been a problem for as long as unhealthy sexual relationships so you could just as easily talk about video games perpetuating violence. Basically, the same question legitimately applies to both: Does fantasy that revels in things we wouldn't want to encounter in the real world - violence, unhealthy relationships, whatever - lead to more (more being defined as relative to what you'd see if that media didn't exist) of the bad thing in the real world.<br /> <br /> There have been plenty of studies, for both violent media and smut. The evidence is inconclusive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28842#post28842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The danger FSoG poses is that anyone that tries to get into actual BDSM relationships with FSoG as a guide is going to hurt themselves (emotionally and/or physically). The problem is that in completely misrepresents what a BDSM relationship actually is and how one is practiced responsibly and safely. Which is an entirely different concern than supernatural beings; werewolves aren't real.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you try to approach joining the army like it's the one in Thor you're in trouble. If you try and approach higher education like it's a raunchy college frat movie you're in trouble.<br /> <br /> Of course anyone who tries to mimic a fantasy book created for entertainment is doing it wrong. That's not a black mark against the entertainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28842#post28842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the evidence is perfectly conclusive. You're just talking about a completely different kind of harm than I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's perfectly conclusive, please cite it. The burden of proof is on you for this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-13-2013, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T05:21:26-08:00","id":29256,"title":"","content":"These games require maturity. Part of this maturity lies with understanding that some behaviours encouraged by the splats displayed are not, in any way, possitive. You're portraying monsters. Struggling or otherwise. In the same way I wouldn't lend 50 Shades of Grey and/or Twilight to an impressionable teenage girl, I wouldn't portray the ugliest aspect of the possessive nature of an Uratha/human relationship, particularly when the former begins to show signs of spiritual degeneration. Because it'll turn ugly. Fast.<br /> <br /> These are a game. If you understand that, the same as you understand that the works cited above are works of fiction, you'll be safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T06:30:58-08:00","id":29278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29231#post29231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fantasy media having a negative effect on the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anybody else remember <i>24</i>? Like, that was a thing that happened. Curiously around the same time that a lot of controversies concerning the United States military and intelligence agencies engaging in acts of torture.<br /> <br /> Culture emerges from beliefs and practices, and we look to culture to inform what our beliefs and practices are. If we didn't, there wouldn't be any point to it.<br /> <br /> You talk about &quot;fantasies&quot;, as if these were stories about slaying dragons, rather than relationships between people.<br /> <br /> In this particular case, abusive relationships that have in-built justifications.<br /> <br /> As if nobody in real life ever tried to justify an abusive relationship. As if justification of abusive relationships, by those within them on either side and by witnesses and bystanders wasn't heartbreakingly common.<br /> <br /> Obviously nobody's in an actual relationship with a vampire or werewolf or whatever, but given that vampires and werewolves are basically metaphors for forms of actual people, and that the justifications can distressingly resemble ones related to actual people...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-13-2013, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T07:31:03-08:00","id":29294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29278#post29278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody else remember <i>24</i>? Like, that was a thing that happened. Curiously around the same time that a lot of controversies concerning the United States military and intelligence agencies engaging in acts of torture.</div> </div> </div> </div> Correlation does not imply causation.<br /> <br /> If you want to say that 24 led to an increase in government sponsored torture or unhealthy werewolf-human relationships leads to an increase in unhealthy human relationships then provide some actual evidence.<br /> <br /> The relationship between media and behaviour is complex, multi-faceted and not fully understood; since pretty much all of the previous times people started saying some form of media or popular narrative was going to cause trouble it turned out to be totally overblown I'm going to remain skeptical until some really good evidence is presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-13-2013, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T08:04:07-08:00","id":29311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29278#post29278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anybody else remember <i>24</i>? Like, that was a thing that happened. Curiously around the same time that a lot of controversies concerning the United States military and intelligence agencies engaging in acts of torture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always suspected the show 24 had a large financial backing by certain branches of the government. It's useful to portray fantasy situations in propaganda to numb the most of the voting block to human rights violations. Not unlike a rapist slipping a woman GHB before attempting to rape her. <br /> <br /> and I'll stop the conspiracy talk now. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T10:48:06-08:00","id":29403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29231#post29231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this actually true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument is a false dichotomy. There's nothing stopping romance novels from both being airport style page turners and treating relationships in a socially responsible way. My wife devours that sort of thing all the time. The burden is on you to demonstrate why you can't have a simple smut novel also be socially responsible in its portrayal of abusive relationships without it turning into War and Peace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fail to see how this is a counter-argument to anything I wrote. </div> </div> </div>Because you're not engaging in the argument I'm making and choosing to conflate it with your previous arguments without any real reasoning as to why they're the same. You're simply making an argument that forces me to deal with your strawman so you don't have to address what I'm actually saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fantasy media having a negative effect on the real world. </div> </div> </div>No. <b>Irresponsible</b> media having a negative effect on the real world. This isn't about genre. We are talking about supernatural romance as a subgenre because that's the topic of the thread. Why the specific element of said topic has a negative effect goes beyond any sort of genre conceit.<br /> <br /> As well, the presence of a negative element in media is not a condemnation of all media, or all media of that genre, or whatever conflation you want to make it out to be. My argument is not, &quot;werewolves as glorifying abusive relationships as healthy is bad, so down with werewolf smut.&quot; My argument is, &quot;werewolves as glorifying abusive relationships as healthy is bad, so lets get that out of werewolf smut.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, the same question legitimately applies to both: </div> </div> </div>That question misses the point. The point is not &quot;more.&quot; The point is how does this fantasy reflect on how our society as a whole treats social issues.<br /> <br /> The whole point of rape culture in feminist theory is not that violence against women in media causes violence against women. The point is that how the media portrays violence against women both reflects our social norms and reinforces them. Rape cultural is about institutionalized prejudices and how society as a whole perpetuates those prejudices; fantasy is simply part of the equation.<br /> <br /> The focus on media expressions of rape culture is not because the media is the &quot;bad actor&quot; or something like that in this perpetuation. The focus on it is because it is the easiest leverage point in changing negative social norms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course anyone who tries to mimic a fantasy book created for entertainment is doing it wrong. </div> </div> </div>Anyone that tries to mimic the negative stuff in fiction is doing it wrong, but anyone trying to mimic the positive stuff in fiction is usually regarded as doing it right.<br /> <br /> As simple example:<br /> <br /> Going around chopping down cherry trees to emulate a myth about George Washington is doing it wrong.<br /> Going around being honest about your misdeeds and mistakes rather than lying to cover them up to emulate a myth about George Washington is doing it right.<br /> <br /> That's the whole point of the story. It is meant to reinforce and encourage a specific type of behavior. &quot;This is just fantasy so copying it means you're doing life wrong,&quot; is a bullshit argument because we use stories and fantasies to communicate social norms and expectations; positive and negative. If stories didn't impact social norms we wouldn't have things like parables, propaganda, and allegory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The burden of proof is on you for this one. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I'm not citing a decade of social theory beyond mentioning its existence. The burden of proof isn't on me, because I don't have to prove myself against your strawman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:00:54-08:00","id":29410,"title":"","content":"Jesus, feminist issues have to be the only damn topic that makes people forget that this is an informal discussion forum mostly about games and not a debate club.<br /> <br /> Okay, not the only issue, but come on.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, when I talk about 24, or Twilight, or whatever, I'm mostly talking about my disgust with it, and the disgust of people whom I know and respect. And people they know. And so on, it goes pretty far.<br /> <br /> All I need to say is that 24 is reprehensible, and that the reason <i>why</i> it's reprehensible is because it's irresponsible at best to glorify torture during a time in which elected and military officials are both sanctioning torture, and varying between trying to cover it up and justify it.<br /> <br /> I don't care if anybody did it because they watched 24, 24 can still fuck right off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:05:39-08:00","id":29413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29410#post29410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus, feminist issues have to be the only damn topic that makes people forget that this is an informal discussion forum mostly about games and not a debate club.</div> </div> </div> </div>You noticed that, too, huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:42:09-08:00","id":29433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29403#post29403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. <b>Irresponsible</b> media having a negative effect on the real world. This isn't about genre. We are talking about supernatural romance as a subgenre because that's the topic of the thread. Why the specific element of said topic has a negative effect goes beyond any sort of genre conceit.<br /> <br /> As well, the presence of a negative element in media is not a condemnation of all media, or all media of that genre, or whatever conflation you want to make it out to be. My argument is not, &quot;werewolves as glorifying abusive relationships as healthy is bad, so down with werewolf smut.&quot; My argument is, &quot;werewolves as glorifying abusive relationships as healthy is bad, so lets get that out of werewolf smut.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> If anyone's using a strawman it's you in the quoted section. I might have used the word fantasy, but since my posts are constantly saying thins like &quot;<b>revels</b> in things we wouldn't want to encounter in the real world - violence, unhealthy relationships&quot;. I think it should be clear that I know we're talking about bad stuff.<br /> <br /> And I know that your argument is for removing abusive relationships rather than the totality of werewolf smut - claiming I don't is a strawman, though I'm inclined to give the benefit of the doubt that it's an accidental one - I quite simply disagree with it. I believe quite strongly that trying to remove anything from the diversity of stories is wrong and thus should only be done when someone's demonstrated a clear and pressing reason for doing so.<br /> <br /> Thus far I remain unsatisfied that there's a reason for removing unhealthy relationships from werewolf smut, or any other kind of smut.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29403#post29403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of rape culture in feminist theory is not that violence against women in media causes violence against women. The point is that how the media portrays violence against women both reflects our social norms and reinforces them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know the theory; I simply disagree with it.<br /> <br /> I disagree that something like the glorification of war in Thor: the Dark World reflects a pro-war social norm.<br /> <br /> I disagree that something like the glorification of war in Thor: the Dark World reinforces a pro-war social norm.<br /> <br /> And the same for absuive werewolf smut.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have asked you and others to provide citations and evidence but thus far you've instead presented your side as though it is self evident. To me the evidence looks inconclusive with studies, for both attitudes towards violence and relationships, often contradicting one another. The historical trend suggests that fears over the effects of media on society are typically worry over nothing.<br /> <br /> Since no one has tried to provide any actual evidence that overly domiment werewolves in smut reinforce unhealthy social norms (reflection would probably be impossible to prove beyond a correlation) I shall continue to believe that this is all worry over nothing.<br /> <br /> Anyone that tries to mimic the negative stuff in fiction is doing it wrong, but anyone trying to mimic the positive stuff in fiction is usually regarded as doing it right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29403#post29403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but I'm not citing a decade of social theory beyond mentioning its existence. The burden of proof isn't on me, because I don't have to prove myself against your strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>The burden of proof is always on the person trying to prove a positive, because proving a negative is essentially impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29413#post29413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You noticed that, too, huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found that any sociology topic tends to do it (there's a big one about historical accuracy on RPG.net right now); also on this forums discussion about metaphysics often turns into a debateing club.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29410#post29410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fundamentally, when I talk about 24, or Twilight, or whatever, I'm mostly talking about my disgust with it, and the disgust of people whom I know and respect. And people they know. And so on, it goes pretty far.<br /> <br /> All I need to say is that 24 is reprehensible, and that the reason <i>why</i> it's reprehensible is because it's irresponsible at best to glorify torture during a time in which elected and military officials are both sanctioning torture, and varying between trying to cover it up and justify it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On both I'll agree with you. I think Edward is a abusive stalker, Bella - <a href=\"http://en.wikiquote.org/wiki/The_Nostalgia_Critic#Top_11_Dumbasses_in_Distress\" target=\"_blank\">well the Nostalgia Critic said it best</a>.<br /> <br /> As for 24, why someone would want to watch a show portraying torture as a heroic thing just confuses me.<br /> <br /> I only disagree when someone says or implies that it shouldn't have been written. I'm glad there's stuff being written for people who don't think like me because they deserve media they enjoy as much as I enjoy mine. And well - &quot;I disapprove of what you say, but I will defend to the death your right to say it.&quot;, not actually said by Voltaire but still true words of wisdom.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't like the unhealthy dominance thing in werewolf smut (admittedly I probably wouldn't read werewolf romance either way) but <i>I don't want it taken out.</i> Instead I'd want books with healthy romances written in addition to the current lot and let people decide what to read. I suspect a lot of people would decide to read both, but that's just a guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-13-2013, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:46:04-08:00","id":29438,"title":"","content":"Christ people,what the hell is this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:51:52-08:00","id":29442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29438#post29438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christ people,what the hell is this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think your Christ or his people had much to do with this. But I could be wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T12:01:06-08:00","id":29446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29433#post29433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I know that your argument is for removing abusive relationships rather than the totality of werewolf smut - claiming I don't is a strawman,...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a strawman if you can't actually express my arguments accurately. Which you're not doing here. Cite one point where I said that abusive relationships have no place in fiction, or even romance literature (werewolf or not).<br /> <br /> When we get past this little sticking point of you not responding to what I'm saying, we can stop talking about this inane strawman bullshit.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> ArcaneArts:<br /> <br /> An Internet forum thread relating to feminist theory. And a tame one at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T12:03:40-08:00","id":29447,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no, I've seen the other ones, and this is nice and all, but we were pretending so much earlier that this was a pleasant thing. Now it's entering gibbering jarbfest territory.<br /> <br /> @Papa Bear: I dunno, some people are going crazy with the wine this time of year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T12:08:05-08:00","id":29452,"title":"","content":"Guys could you take it to rpg.net? I don't think this board is improved much by sociology fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T12:34:07-08:00","id":29462,"title":"","content":"I'm confused as to how the books glorify it if it's mentioned in the context of being a horrifying thing that could happen. It sounds like it would cause degeneration and be traumatic. It wouldn't be a good thing.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like how it's pretty outright stated in multiple places that Vampires can be or are horrifically abusive with their Ghouls, and that's bad. I'm under the impression that this sentence about Uratha is essentially making the same point, that they can be awful and angry and it's not a good thing.<br /> <br /> If anything, it makes the point that it's incredibly selfish to try to have a relationship with somebody when they're under the threat of you murdering them because you get irrationally angry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T13:22:17-08:00","id":29490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29462#post29462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused as to how the books glorify it if it's mentioned in the context of being a horrifying thing that could happen. It sounds like it would cause degeneration and be traumatic. It wouldn't be a good thing.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like how it's pretty outright stated in multiple places that Vampires can be or are horrifically abusive with their Ghouls, and that's bad. I'm under the impression that this sentence about Uratha is essentially making the same point, that they can be awful and angry and it's not a good thing.<br /> <br /> If anything, it makes the point that it's incredibly selfish to try to have a relationship with somebody when they're under the threat of you murdering them because you get irrationally angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought too, but I wanted to check what other people thought, in case I had missed some part in a Forsaken book that pulled the Hauptman effect: <a href=\"http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/p/fangs-lexicon.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/p/fangs-lexicon.html</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/2011/10/abuse-as-true-love-in-paranormal.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEipxujqNMWsE0IeEnt8-IeCE64psIfLzxkLgdozZpu3Sd_E4hWHhzK3_kR7tPmxsFNlQrFTEwAcTp_wi3KG4BZb7zV9R-OZb-R7UFdFTcz2uKbv53L-YHugppbkZPBpovkdLxgq3hvsbOpN/w1200-h630-p-k-no-nu/\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/2011/10/abuse-as-true-love-in-paranormal.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Abuse as True Love in Paranormal Romance </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/2011/10/abuse-as-true-love-in-paranormal.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.fangsforthefantasy.com/2011/10/abuse-as-true-love-in-paranormal.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There are a lot of tropes in paranormal romance that consistently raise their ugly heads - many of which we explain in our Lexicon ... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T13:25:29-08:00","id":29493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29447#post29447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no, I've seen the other ones, and this is nice and all, but we were pretending so much earlier that this was a pleasant thing. Now it's entering gibbering jarbfest territory.<br /> <br /> @Papa Bear: I dunno, some people are going crazy with the wine this time of year.</div> </div> </div> </div>They over-fermented the grapes again, huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T13:38:44-08:00","id":29500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29446#post29446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a strawman if you can't actually express my arguments accurately. Which you're not doing here. Cite one point where I said that abusive relationships have no place in fiction, or even romance literature (werewolf or not).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right here: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29403#post29403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is, &quot;werewolves as glorifying abusive relationships as healthy is bad, <u>so lets get that out of werewolf smut.</u>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29462#post29462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused as to how the books glorify it if it's mentioned in the context of being a horrifying thing that could happen. It sounds like it would cause degeneration and be traumatic. It wouldn't be a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't. Everyone agreed that Forskaen doesn't glorify abusive relationships and since everyone agreed that part of the conversation ended. Now we're talking about different werewolf books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-13-2013, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T14:28:33-08:00","id":29525,"title":"","content":"Ah, alright, my bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T14:33:15-08:00","id":29530,"title":"","content":"Ok Kings Raven.<br /> <br /> You realize there is a massive difference between &quot;Lets get glorifying abusive relationships out of werewolf smut&quot; and &quot;Lets get abusive relationships out of werewolf smut completely,&quot; right?<br /> <br /> Nowhere have I made the argument that you cannot include abusive relationships in werewolf smut, or that simply putting abusive relationships in werewolf smut you're &quot;doing it wrong.&quot; Hence all the talk of glorification, irresponsibility, and all that.<br /> <br /> Claiming that quote equates to me saying that abusive relationships have no place in fiction, is as valid me characterizing your stance as anyone that doesn't write about abusive relationships needs to be forced to so that they are contributing properly to diversity in the market.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T14:53:37-08:00","id":29543,"title":"","content":"Ok so I looked through a bunch of pages in the site posted. I say they are less concerned about abusive relationships and just complain about anything no matter what. I mean even when it comes to race you can't win. <br /> From the site: <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#CC0033\"><b>Token</b>:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Including a single marginalised character for the sake of </span></span><b>Inclusion Cookies</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the portrayal is normally very stereotyped, exists to serve the privileged protagonists or is otherwise annoying, offensive or aggravating </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#CC0033\">Minority Decay</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Sometimes a show starts and we get very eager \u2013 why the pilot has several POC! And GBLT people! And disabled people and older people \u2013 why the diversity is stunning!</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But as the series progresses, these characters start to die off. Or spend a lot of time hanging around in the background doing nothing. Or sometimes just falling into a plot hole and not being seen for episodes at a time; before you know it, all that potential has dried up to nothing. The most likely cause of this is</span></span><b>Tokenism. </b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#CC0033\"><b>Inclusion Cookies</b>:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Including a marginalised character or referencing marginalised people in order to prove how inclusive and forward thinking a series is (or to shut up marginalised people complaining about </span></span><b>Erasure</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) The inclusion is normally a </span></span><b>Token</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and extremely stereotyped. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#CC0033\"><b>Bonnie</b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Aka White Girl Dipped in Chocolate \u2013 when a </span></span><b>Token</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> inclusion has no cultural or historical markers, they have dark skin for </span></span><b>Inclusions cookies</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> but if you closed your eyes there'd be nothing differentiating them from the white cast. <br /> <br /> With these kind of ideas how could you possible please these people? And it seems their standards for female characters are ten times worse. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T15:13:18-08:00","id":29552,"title":"","content":"It's very easy to win, in these cases. Don't write token characters. Almost all of these are about tokenism in one form or another.<br /> <br /> Well, for token: You can write minority characters without including them only because they're minorities. You can write them without being stereotypical.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's too much to ask nor particularly hard.<br /> <br /> For Minority Decay, don't kill off all the people of color or banish them unimportant land. Emphasis on <b>all</b> because that's the key point. When practically all the people of color or LGBT characters get killed off, leaving the white cis whatever protagonists, that's where one might call foul. The two feed into eachother as far as Tokenism goes, because Token characters aren't terribly compelling.<br /> <br /> Inclusion Cookies is when the token character was included specifically to address complaints about erasure or the lack of diversity. I don't really think this one needs to be explained, but it's basically, if you've been told that your show or book lacks diversity or whatever, including a character who is a stereotype and solely for the purpose of assuaging those complaints is tokenism and insulting.<br /> <br /> Bonnie: This one might be a bit trickier, but it's essentially the idea that diversity of skin tone with no acknowledgement of culture or background or anything like that is just another form of tokenism, and that if you're including people of color, it pays to acknowledge the fact that they are people of color, without reminding the reader of it every five seconds. I feel like this one can be a pitfall, because if you think too hard about it, you'll feel stilted, but if you don't think about it at all, it's paying lip service to the idea of diversity rather than actual diversity.<br /> <br /> I really think there's a tendency for people to overreact to this sort of criticism as &quot;It's impossible to please you people!&quot; but that's a mistake. You wouldn't want to write a cliche character for any other reason, so why would you want to write one who is LGBT or a person of color?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T15:22:56-08:00","id":29564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SirPants</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29452#post29452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys could you take it to rpg.net? I don't think this board is improved much by sociology fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>........... This.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T15:24:51-08:00","id":29568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29493#post29493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They over-fermented the grapes again, huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or swapped out the wine for Absinthe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T15:27:02-08:00","id":29572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29552#post29552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think there's a tendency for people to overreact to this sort of criticism as &quot;It's impossible to please you people!&quot; but that's a mistake. You wouldn't want to write a cliche character for any other reason, so why would you want to write one who is LGBT or a person of color?</div> </div> </div> </div>BAsically this. A person's culture or ethnicity or sexuality is a part of who they are, it should inform and influence their character development, but not necessarily overrule it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T15:30:23-08:00","id":29575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29530#post29530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You realize there is a massive difference between &quot;Lets get glorifying abusive relationships out of werewolf smut&quot; and &quot;Lets get abusive relationships out of werewolf smut completely,&quot; right?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I disagree that there is a massive difference. To both of them my answer is the same: Show me the harm this is causing; until I see genuine harm I disprove of trying to get anything out of stories/smut/whatever.<br /> <br /> 2) I have been talking about the glorification of abusive relationships since the beginning. My second post in this entire thread contains this nugget:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=28617#post28617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I kinda share zap's confusion. I don't read romance either, but the idea books <b>revealing</b> in romantic troupes that should be avoided in the real world just seems... normal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>My terrible spelling aside, 'revelling' means celebrating, aka glorification.<br /> <br /> Or if you must hear me use the world glorification, how about this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29433#post29433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that something like the <b>glorification</b> of war in Thor: the Dark World reflects a pro-war social norm.<br /> <br /> I disagree that something like the <b>glorification</b> of war in Thor: the Dark World reinforces a pro-war social norm.<br /> <br /> And the <b>same</b> for absuive werewolf smut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or this one from the post imediately before the word strawman entered this discussion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29231#post29231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just like any film that realistically portrays war hits a different niche to a simple action flick <u>where violence is awesome</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div> It might not be the word glorification, but I would assume that &quot;violence is awesome&quot; can be treated as roughly synonymous with &quot;glorifying violence&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I will admit that I misread you in my previous post; but I always knew that your view was specific to the glorification and I will also admit that <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29433#post29433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I know that your argument is for removing abusive relationships rather than the totality of werewolf smut</div> </div> </div> </div> should have had the word glorified in there; but considering that I have consistently refereed to the glorification of war or unhealthy sexual relationship throughout my posts here I would have thought it was clear from context that I knew this discussion was about the glorification of abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-13-2013, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T19:10:49-08:00","id":29661,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I kind of want to ask about The Birth of a Nation.<br /> <br /> ... Might as well just do it: what does The Kings Raven think of aforementioned film? Does it have anything to do with actual incidents of racism? Should it not be considered according to those terms?<br /> <br /> Or is it just harmless escapist fantasy for scared angry white people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T19:21:37-08:00","id":29665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29543#post29543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say they are less concerned about abusive relationships and just complain about anything no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? 'Cause there seems to be a consistent theme in the examples you've provided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With these kind of ideas how could you possible please these people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have more than one minority character. Don't resort to stereotyping. Don't arbitrarily reduce the number of minority characters either through removing them or forgetting them. Don't put them in a context which seems to be about trumpeting them as an example of the shows awareness rather than because the character serves the story. Don't neglect to be aware of how cultural context differentiates the experience of minority characters.<br /> <br /> Even some of these can slide a little; look at Jodie Landon from Daria. She's the only black girl in the cast because part of that show's point is criticizing that kind of plastic suburbia which is almost uniformly white by design, and characters internally acknowledge how messed up that is (including occasions where other characters actually stroll her out as a demonstration of &quot;progressive diversity&quot; in much the manner that the cited example suggests).<br /> <br /> This is really not difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T22:00:22-08:00","id":29727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29575#post29575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that there is a massive difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're resorting to a lot of, &quot;well I just disagree.&quot; Fine. You disagree. But your disagreement doesn't change the fact that our culture is messed up when it comes to how it treats minorities in entertainment. You can proclaim all you want that it is on everyone else to prove things to your satisfaction; but that just sounds like an excuse to avoid looking at the evidence that's we've known about for decades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or if you must hear me use the world glorification, how about this: </div> </div> </div>What glorification of war exactly are you talking about? Thor, through both of the new movies, is shown realizing that the heavy-handed interventionist warfare he was raised to see as virtuous and positive is not all it was cracked up to be. Thor grows completely disillusioned with the &quot;glory&quot; of war and begins to see violence as a last resort to be used with maximum restraint. In the first movie he charges off into battle convinced he can bash all this people's problems into dust. In the second movie he ends a battle as quickly as possible by a show of force and then demanding peaceful surrender over slaughtering his enemies. It's hard to see a movie where the main character's primary development is realizing that his simplistic views of war and glory are naive and misguided, as being a movie that's all about how awesome war is.<br /> <br /> And all of that out of a movie that's 99% excuse for awesome comic book action and sexy men.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It might not be the word glorification, but I would assume that &quot;violence is awesome&quot; can be treated as roughly synonymous with &quot;glorifying violence&quot;. </div> </div> </div>As, culturally, most people accept that there are ethical applications of violence, the glorification of violence alone isn't problematic. The glorification of violence that we recognize as unethical is when it gets problematic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will admit that I misread you in my previous post; but I always knew that your view was specific to the glorification and I will also admit that should have had the word glorified in there; but considering that I have consistently refereed to the glorification of war or unhealthy sexual relationship throughout my posts here I would have thought it was clear from context that I knew this discussion was about the glorification of abuse. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that whether or not you know this is about the glorification of abuse or not, your arguments all seem to hinge on ignoring that to conflate different points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T22:35:42-08:00","id":29751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29568#post29568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or swapped out the wine for Absinthe</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, hadn't thought of that....looks like it could be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T01:28:36-08:00","id":29806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29661#post29661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I kind of want to ask about The Birth of a Nation.<br /> <br /> ... Might as well just do it: what does The Kings Raven think of aforementioned film? Does it have anything to do with actual incidents of racism? Should it not be considered according to those terms?<br /> <br /> Or is it just harmless escapist fantasy for scared angry white people?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard of that film until now, so going I'm going by the Wikipedia page.<br /> <br /> As I've been saying all along &quot;show me the harm&quot;; I would say that being a major part in forming the Klan's &quot;second era&quot; undoubtedly qualifies as harm.<br /> <br /> Also, I think your choice of example isn't fair to the debate at hand. We're talking about books written by women for a primarily women audience. If you want to use a race example use something created by an African American for an African American audience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29727#post29727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're resorting to a lot of, &quot;well I just disagree.&quot; Fine. You disagree. But your disagreement doesn't change the fact that our culture is messed up when it comes to how it treats minorities in entertainment. You can proclaim all you want that it is on everyone else to prove things to your satisfaction; but that just sounds like an excuse to avoid looking at the evidence that's we've known about for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly I'm saying I don't think glorification of unhealthy romance should to be taken out of anything. That's a completely different argument to saying our culture is or isn't messed up. I have been consistent in saying that if there is a clear causative link between glorifying negatives and actual problems then I'll support removing them; but that topic has been extensively studied and the evidence is inconclusive. Is it really that hard to imagine that someone might look at the same evidence and come to a different conclusion? Or that hard to say so without making remarks about my character?<br /> <br /> Secondly, I think one of the best things that could be done for the way women are portrayed in media is to support female authors. If it turns out they want to write abusive werewolf smut then so be it. I'll support that.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, I do not think it is <b>ever</b> unreasonable to ask someone to provide evidence to support their views.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29727#post29727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What glorification of war exactly are you talking about? Thor, through both of the new movies, is shown realizing that the heavy-handed interventionist warfare he was raised to see as virtuous and positive is not all it was cracked up to be. Thor grows completely disillusioned with the &quot;glory&quot; of war and begins to see violence as a last resort to be used with maximum restraint. In the first movie he charges off into battle convinced he can bash all this people's problems into dust. In the second movie he ends a battle as quickly as possible by a show of force and then demanding peaceful surrender over slaughtering his enemies. It's hard to see a movie where the main character's primary development is realizing that his simplistic views of war and glory are naive and misguided, as being a movie that's all about how awesome war is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Relative to actual war that is glorification; despite Thor's objections the primary emotion evoked by the war is <b>awesome</b> not horror. The battle scenes are set to dramatic music, there is no blood or gore, we never see anything from the low-ranked soldiers point of view.<br /> <br /> Where's the stuff about dehumanisaton, crippling PTSD, being treated as a disposable tool by the officers?<br /> <br /> Though we're drifting off topic in Thor. Why not pick another example, would Inglorious Bastards work for you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29727#post29727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that whether or not you know this is about the glorification of abuse or not, your arguments all seem to hinge on ignoring that to conflate different points.</div> </div> </div> </div>What different points? Glorification of war and glorification of abuse?<br /> <br /> My argument is very simple; until it can be demonstrated that these novels are causing significant harm I reject that there's any need to change them. Everything else has been about whether that harm exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-14-2013, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T05:26:32-08:00","id":29848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29806#post29806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that being a major part in forming the Klan's &quot;second era&quot; undoubtedly qualifies as harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind directing me to the proofs provided for that fact that convinced you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about books written by women for a primarily women audience. If you want to use a race example use something created by an African American for an African American audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, the sad thing is, I probably could find some kind of essay or novel written by early- to mid-19th century American black people, whether free or slave, arguing in favour of slavery.<br /> <br /> Or probably some stuff involving black Republicans.<br /> <br /> I just <i>really</i> don't want to trawl through that shit.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, pervasiveness of a toxic social element that leads to people who are harmed by that element being conditioned to view it as a good or natural thing does not validate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T06:53:48-08:00","id":29880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29848#post29848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you mind directing me to the proofs provided for that fact that convinced you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course.<br /> <br /> I started with the Wikipedia page for birth of a nation which said that <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to a 2002 article in the Los Angeles Times, the film facilitated the refounding of the Ku Klux Klan in the 1920s.<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Birth_of_a_Nation#cite_note-34\" target=\"_blank\">[34]</a></sup> As late as the 1970s, the Ku Klux Klan continued to use the film as a recruitment tool.</div> </div> </div> </div> I knew about the Klan from just general knowledge, so that was sufficient for me to believe <i>Birth of a Nation</i> caused real harm; provided that this was true. So I did some quick googling and it wasn't hard to find agreement such as this <a href=\"http://www.historynet.com/the-birth-of-a-nation-when-hollywood-glorified-the-kkk.htm\" target=\"_blank\">history.net</a> article, or <a href=\"http://michigantoday.umich.edu/2009/06/story.php?id=7485\" target=\"_blank\">this article by Frank Bever</a>. Rodger Ebery, who I generally trust on matters relating to film, also said it was considered to <a href=\"http://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/great-movie-the-birth-of-a-nation-1915\" target=\"_blank\">racist when it was first published</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically; it's not what I'd consider scholar grade research but Wikipedia's claim that Birth of a Nation was instrimental in the foundation of the second Klan seems to be supported and I think we can all agree that the Klan did a lot of horrible horrible things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29848#post29848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suffice to say, pervasiveness of a toxic social element that leads to people who are harmed by that element being conditioned to view it as a good or natural thing does not validate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes... that wasn't my point. What I was saying is that you should use a like-for-like comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T07:35:30-08:00","id":29900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>zap rowsdower:</b><br /> With these kind of ideas how could you possible please these people? And it seems their standards for female characters are ten times worse. </div> </div> </div>The number of books/media that <i>do</i> please them ought to clue you in that it's possible. (And the fact that their criticisms routinely do not prevent them from liking what they criticise).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T08:24:16-08:00","id":29922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29806#post29806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly I'm saying I don't think glorification of unhealthy romance should to be taken out of anything. That's a completely different argument to saying our culture is or isn't messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the &quot;harm&quot; you keep wanting to be shown is that those two things are linked. Again, see pretty much all the sociology that explains why we don't just have toxic levels of sexual abuse, assault, and rape in our society, but also huge amounts of victims blaming, shaming, and excusing of attackers.<br /> <br /> Why do we live in a culture that makes women fear coming forward about what's happened to them? Why do we live in a culture was a rapist facing sentencing has people actually making the arguments that said rapist should get a light sentence because his life is getting ruined because of a &quot;mistake?&quot;<br /> <br /> If you have a better or more convincing theory than rape culture, lets hear it. Lets hear your support for why a different model explains this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have been consistent in saying that if there is a clear causative link between glorifying negatives and actual problems then I'll support removing them; but that topic has been extensively studied and the evidence is inconclusive. </div> </div> </div>Please cite a proof of this affirmative declaration. If you're all about people backing up what they say, what's yours?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it really that hard to imagine that someone might look at the same evidence and come to a different conclusion? </div> </div> </div>Hard? No.<br /> <br /> Depressing? Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, I think one of the best things that could be done for the way women are portrayed in media is to support female authors. If it turns out they want to write abusive werewolf smut then so be it. I'll support that. </div> </div> </div>Also back this up. Why should the demographics of the creator matter compared to the nature of their content? If I care about changing how women are portrayed in the media, why should I favor women authors that don't change things over men that do? I'm all for supporting women authors but they don't get a pass for being women; if they write crap I'm not buying it.<br /> <br /> If change is going to happen by voting with my wallet, than I should vote based on the issue at hand, not the demographics of who's saying it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thirdly, I do not think it is <b>ever</b> unreasonable to ask someone to provide evidence to support their views. </div> </div> </div>It is unreasonable to continually pester someone for evidence because you don't agree with the theory their evidence is based on though. If you know enough about rape culture theory to have a serious refutation of it, you should know what my evidence is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Relative to actual war that is glorification; despite Thor's objections the primary emotion evoked by the war is <b>awesome</b> not horror. The battle scenes are set to dramatic music, there is no blood or gore, we never see anything from the low-ranked soldiers point of view. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but how is this not just stretching the word &quot;glorification&quot; to meaningless extremes?<br /> <br /> Besides the fact that the dark elf/Asgardian war is actually shown as an extremely brutal affair (fake blood and gore doesn't inherently make something less glorification, as you essentially point out by bringing up Tarantino), not seeing things from a common soldiers perspective doesn't prove a work is glorifying anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not pick another example, would Inglorious Bastards work for you? </div> </div> </div>Work for me for what? Make your case for yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What different points? </div> </div> </div>Trying to tie an anti-censorship &quot;diversity&quot; argument into this. Trying to tie in small picture studies about the direct impact of things like violence as evidence against larger sociological theories. Trying to make supporting toxic cultural elements an act of feminism/egalitarianism just because it is written by a women. Trying to pick specific films/works to try and make the case that I somehow think X is acceptable so I'm wrong about Y (the subject of war vs. violence against women is irrelevant as a specific).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My argument is very simple; until it can be demonstrated that these novels are causing significant harm I reject that there's any need to change them. Everything else has been about whether that harm exists. </div> </div> </div>The harm exists in a culture that is doing substantive harm to the physical and mental health to its female population, and the normalization of the social prejudices that create that harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T09:30:41-08:00","id":29957,"title":"","content":"Amahan Iduth forgive me. What have I started?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T09:04:26-08:00","id":31013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/28055-gender-dynamics-in-forsaken?p=29957#post29957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amahan Iduth forgive me. What have I started?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the forums should come with a disclaimer about gender issues, sexuality, religion, and political affiliation. It's like lighting a fuse into a powder keg: it <b>will </b>blow up at some point, it's just a matter of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T14:41:33-08:00","id":31905,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Since this conversation no longer has anything to do with Forsaken it's being closed, if you want to continue the discussion in the Off Topic forums you may.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}